From f40e4e7db1301bfde49c19835388b3c91730c05c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Morris <felixmorris.biz@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 14:33:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add macOS and PS4 support

Recognise emblem requests by their path (/u<hex>.slot_<n>) on a Demonware
host rather than a hardcoded PS3 hostname, so the PS4 and PS5 releases work
without knowing their content-server hostname in advance. Detect the emblem
blob's byte order per capture, since the PS3 writes big-endian and the PC and
PS4/PS5 releases write little-endian.

On macOS, keep captures in Application Support for .app bundles instead of
inside the bundle, create the data directory before writing to it, close
tunnel sockets rather than leaking descriptors, list every candidate LAN
address so Internet Sharing works, and add a Finder launcher, a build script
and a Quit button.

Also fix path traversal via control-panel group names, origin-form proxy
requests, missing socket timeouts and silent proxy startup failures.
